ment_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 840, "end": 986, "text": "They had met in Barcelona, where James had been attending a conference on international trade, and Marià had been representing the Catalan region."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 987, "end": 1073, "text": "It was a chance encounter, but one that had changed the course of their lives forever."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1074, "end": 1183, "text": "James leaned down to kiss her cheek, and Marià whispered something in his ear, her voice husky and confident."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1184, "end": 1263, "text": "James chuckled, his eyes crinkling at the corners, and replied in hushed tones."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1264, "end": 1346, "text": "The group of young men looked on, envious of the easy intimacy between the couple."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1347, "end": 1509, "text": "As the night wore on, James and Marià made their way to the podium, where James was scheduled to give a speech on the importance of Irish-Spanish trade relations."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1510, "end": 1648, "text": "Marià, ever the supportive partner, stood by his side, her presence a reminder to the crowd of the strong bonds between their two nations."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1649, "end": 1753, "text": "As James began to speak, his words were met with applause and cheers, and Marià's eyes shone with pride."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1754, "end": 1874, "text": "It was a moment that James would never forget, a moment that solidified their partnership, both in politics and in life."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "James Fitz Edmond Cotter", "scope": "Spouse", "claim": "James Fitz Edmond Cotter married Eleanora Plunkett in 1778.", "answer